            "text": "{\"primary_meaning\":\"Divine protection, strength, and a secure refuge for believers.\",\"primary_basis\":[\"Proverbs 18:10\",\"Psalm 61:3\",\"2 Samuel 22:51\"],\"alternatives\":[{\"meaning\":\"Human pride, rebellion, and arrogant self-reliance against God.\",\"basis\":[\"Genesis 11:1-9\",\"Isaiah 2:15\",\"Isaiah 30:25\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Spiritual vigilance, warning, and prophetic foresight (watchtower).\",\"basis\":[\"Habakkuk 2:1\",\"Ezekiel 33:2-6\",\"Isaiah 21:8\"],\"prominence\":\"common\"},{\"meaning\":\"Spiritual preparation and counting the cost of discipleship.\",\"basis\":[\"Luke 14:28\"],\"prominence\":\"minority\"}],\"has_settled_consensus\":true,\"confidence\":\"high\",\"notes\":\"The symbol of a tower is context-dependent in scripture, most prominently representing God's ultimate protection and security for the righteous. Conversely, when built by humans as a monument (such as the Tower of Babel), it serves as a classic symbol of human hubris, pride, and defiance of God. It also frequently appears as a metaphor for a prophet's vigilance.\"}",
